{"View Grants Global Manage: canManage() is used by the top-level group creation path through requireManage(), but this check accepts the all-groups view scope. A realm admin granted only group viewing through the new resource type can create groups, which crosses the intended authorization boundary.": 0.9636608362197876, "Resource Ids Become Group Ids: The loop uses the authorization resource id as both the permission lookup key and the returned group id. hasPermission looks up resources by name, and the user provider later filters UserGroupMembershipEntity.groupId with this set, so an admin with view-members on a group can get empty user search and count results even though the group permission exists.": 0.7305818200111389, "Global View Is Rechecked Per Group: The removed canViewGlobal shortcut changes all-groups VIEW from a list-wide permission into a per-group resource check. When a group already has a resource for a member or membership-only scope, canView(group) can return false even though canView() is true, so the group list silently drops allowed groups after provider pagination.": 0.9269026517868042, "Subgroups Ignore Global View: requireView(group) can pass because the caller has type-level all-groups VIEW, but each child is now filtered only with canView(child). If a child has a per-group resource for another scope, the child can be hidden from a caller who is allowed to view all groups.": 0.9512917995452881, "Unknown Resource Types Now Throw: This public schema helper used to return null for unsupported resource types, but the new switch turns the same input into an IllegalStateException. Any extension or caller that probes a non-core admin resource type now gets a server error instead of the previous not-created result.": 0.9150201082229614}